This product will (when code lands) include and build upon:

- OpenIPC devourer — userspace RTL8812AU/CU/EU driver, GPL-2.0.
  https://github.com/OpenIPC/devourer
- libusb — USB access library, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
  https://github.com/libusb/libusb

Design and calibration groundwork reuses values, formats, and control discipline
from (all GPL-2.0, credited for provenance — no code copied into this repo yet):

- waybeam_wfb_ng `link_controller` — adaptive MCS/bitrate control constants and
  the reactive-demote / probe-promote / flap-freeze state machine (§13).
- waybeam_venc — the live encoder-bitrate HTTP API surface (§13.6).
- Realtek rtl88x2eu/cu driver — the `PHY_REG_PG.txt` per-rate TX-power table row
  format, reused as the per-MCS power data structure (§14).

The adaptive link layer (§13–14) is lifted-and-adapted from the above, not novel.
The novel contributions of waybeam-link are the diversity+ARQ transport and the
opaque passive-latch session model. See README.md.
